        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-residues_identify_digit",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED by walking all 256 ordered pairs from the sixteen hex digits: the two residues (mod 6, mod 9) identify a digit uniquely — no two of the sixteen share both — and the pair space is 18, two larger than the sixteen it must separate."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "((List.range 16).all (fun a => (List.range 16).all (fun b => (!((a % 6 == b % 6) && (a % 9 == b % 9))) || (a == b)))) ∧ (2 * 9 = 18) ∧ (18 % 6 = 0) ∧ (18 % 9 = 0) ∧ (18 - 16 = 2)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem residues_identify_digit : ((List.range 16).all (fun a => (List.range 16).all (fun b => (!((a % 6 == b % 6) && (a % 9 == b % 9))) || (a == b)))) ∧ (2 * 9 = 18) ∧ (18 % 6 = 0) ∧ (18 % 9 = 0) ∧ (18 - 16 = 2) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-crt_pairs_are_a_bijection",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED over every one of the 63 residues: x ↦ (x mod 7, x mod 9) yields 63 distinct pairs, so the correspondence is a bijection and no residue collides with another."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(((List.range 63).map (fun x => (x % 7) * 9 + (x % 9))).eraseDups.length = 63)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem crt_pairs_are_a_bijection : (((List.range 63).map (fun x => (x % 7) * 9 + (x % 9))).eraseDups.length = 63) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-fused_units_are_the_orbit_squared",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED by counting units across all 63 residues: the fused ring has exactly 36 units, which is 6·6 — the vortex orbit length times the rosette orbit length, each of those six counted over its own whole ring."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(((List.range 63).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 63 == 1)).length = 36) ∧ (6 * 6 = 36) ∧ (((List.range 9).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 9 == 1)).length = 6) ∧ (((List.range 7).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 7 == 1)).length = 6)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem fused_units_are_the_orbit_squared : (((List.range 63).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 63 == 1)).length = 36) ∧ (6 * 6 = 36) ∧ (((List.range 9).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 9 == 1)).length = 6) ∧ (((List.range 7).filter (fun a => a > 0 && Nat.gcd a 7 == 1)).length = 6) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
